{"title":"De Longchamps point","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The title of this article has been capitalized due to technical restrictions. The correct title should be '</i><b>de Longchamps point'</b><i>.</i></dd></dl>\n<table style=\"border:thin solid black;padding:5px;float:right;margin:10px;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"border:thin solid gray;\">\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/2/8e2fc3535addbb951f5f9621f4305542f0734745.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(44,60)--(44,-10)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(44,0),blue+dashed); draw((44,60)--(22,-5),blue+dashed); draw((44,-10)--(6.5,10),blue+dashed); label(&quot;H&quot;,(24,0),(1,1)); dot((24,0)); draw((22,30)--(44,14),red); draw((22,-5)--(34,46),red); draw((44,25)--(18,25),red); dot((29,25)); label(&quot;C&quot;,(29,25),(1,1)); draw(Circle((29,25),25),dashed); dot((34,50)); label(&quot;L&quot;,(34,50),(1,1)); [/asy]\" width=\"195\" height=\"252\" />\t\n</p>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><div class=\"magnify\" style=\"float: right;\">\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Enlarge.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/15px-Enlarge.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"15\" height=\"9\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/23px-Enlarge.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/30px-Enlarge.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure></div> The de Longchamps <br />point (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />) is the the <br /><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Orthocenter\" title=\"Orthocenter\">orthocenter</a> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />) reflected <br /> through the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcenter\" title=\"Circumcenter\">circumcenter</a><br /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />).\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The <b>de Longchamps point</b> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Reflection_(mathematics)&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Reflection (mathematics) (page does not exist)\">reflection</a> of the triangle's <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Orthocenter\" title=\"Orthocenter\">orthocenter</a> through its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcenter\" title=\"Circumcenter\">circumcenter</a>.\n</p><p>The point is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Collinear\" title=\"Collinear\">collinear</a> with the orthocenter and circumcenter.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#de_Longchamps_point\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">de Longchamps point</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#De_Longchamps_circle\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">De Longchamps circle</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#De_Longchamps_line\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">De Longchamps line</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"de_Longchamps_point\">de Longchamps point</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=De_Longchamps_point&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: de Longchamps point\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Longchamps.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4a/Longchamps.png/450px-Longchamps.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"511\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/4a/Longchamps.png 1.5x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><i><b>Definition 1</b></i>\n</p><p>The de Longchamps point of a triangle is the radical center of the power circles of the triangle. Prove that De Longchamps point lies on Euler line.\n</p><p>We call A-power circle of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> the circle centered at the midpoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/2/612426ac83325710242dd421d0f842053ceb4018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_A = AA&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"19\" /> The other two circles are defined symmetrically. \n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a85d06eddefb2860ce839ba7182b844b65f5e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H, O,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be orthocenter, circumcenter, and De Longchamps point, respectively.\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b179fc3cbe5f135dece01c0601a6db2be93ad866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B-$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />power circle by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/e/bdeecb1debe93d1648359e884c564a194ec11c9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_B, C-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />power circle by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d96676fa5e7076b824d19da27fec2af6d99f1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_C, D = \\omega_B \\cap \\omega_C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5f7dc1d5eeb07dd8b66defdcdc5e92fafab1d61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = BC, b = AC, c = AB.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" /> WLOG, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9e8a9a48259c6d1b3e1ca2121dabbf2fcc57098.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ge b \\ge c.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/feb2994cf26e21cb51b85b0e488425cab2e7dab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> the projection of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccb9a009c1c0d9c80ca62145818c8ffcc6125f54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;C&#39;, E = D_t.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>We will prove that radical axes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b179fc3cbe5f135dece01c0601a6db2be93ad866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B-$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />power and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/93875d269236b50fb99cd99249c0fa9b87eb6f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />power cicles is symmetric to altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3ddf9a5fa2fca5c4787d4f989af0eef1387bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c79ddff6b45c6ad853d03d6231fdf0fba5ededb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O.$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> Further, we will conclude that the point of intersection of the radical axes, symmetrical to the heights with respect to O, is symmetrical to the point of intersection of the heights <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c79ddff6b45c6ad853d03d6231fdf0fba5ededb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O.$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the crosspoint of the center line of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b179fc3cbe5f135dece01c0601a6db2be93ad866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B-$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />power and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/93875d269236b50fb99cd99249c0fa9b87eb6f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />power circles and there radical axis. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b3bcc8ccbe6e817dedca48708d453fc3f87f879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;C&#39; = \\frac {a}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"34\" /> We use claim and get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/c/a4c7a4fee33cb23de638becf40d83b2e189fc0a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[C&#39;E =  \\frac {a}{4} + \\frac {R_C^2 – R_B^2}{a}.\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/7/517782adad3048607d27ff0a5e45d9fb9d3326ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4c05d7bcc9cc778be31ccb9012cc3672073fa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> are the medians, so \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a902d6ea14ebe6d188451af29481de8870ebe56d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R_B^2 = \\frac {a^2}{2}+ \\frac {c^2}{2} – \\frac {b^2}{4}, R_C^2 = \\frac {a^2}{2}+ \\frac {b^2}{2} – \\frac {c^2}{4} \\implies C&#39;E =  \\frac {a}{4} + \\frac {3(b^2 – c^2)}{4a}.\\]\" width=\"503\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>We use Claim some times and get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/3/f3395f6cad3449fd9fbd3a5a7cd669c32b414d4d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[C&#39;A_t =  \\frac {a}{4} – \\frac {b^2 – c^2}{4a}, A_tO_t =  \\frac {a}{2} – 2 C&#39;A_t = \\frac {b^2 – c^2}{2a} \\implies\\]\" width=\"378\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/718ef0a57812063866ca13ebc8cf3483e01f7525.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[O_t L_t = C&#39;E – C&#39;A_t - A_t O_t = \\frac {b^2 – c^2}{2a}  = A_t O_t = H_t O_t \\implies\\]\" width=\"440\" height=\"39\" />\nradical axes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b179fc3cbe5f135dece01c0601a6db2be93ad866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B-$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />power and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/93875d269236b50fb99cd99249c0fa9b87eb6f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />power cicles is symmetric to altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3ddf9a5fa2fca5c4787d4f989af0eef1387bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c79ddff6b45c6ad853d03d6231fdf0fba5ededb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O.$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Similarly radical axes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/722563bfd5e279d3115d6962b904fcdc85cce7f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A-$\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />power and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b179fc3cbe5f135dece01c0601a6db2be93ad866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B-$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />power cicles is symmetric to altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/0/fd0a7235440e6e51d63865a9bb199193fbcc80d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> radical axes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/722563bfd5e279d3115d6962b904fcdc85cce7f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A-$\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />power and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/93875d269236b50fb99cd99249c0fa9b87eb6f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />power cicles is symmetric to altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfc6159e268a0f5d736eca73477c99a13209da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c79ddff6b45c6ad853d03d6231fdf0fba5ededb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O.$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />\nTherefore the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of intersection of the radical axes, symmetrical to the heights with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/b/56b4c0ef575d9ec02ec52379f2cc6f6fa28acc13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> is symmetrical to the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> of intersection of the heights with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb4bd395d001accd04e9d59d8df352a9ff9f7e79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O \\implies \\vec {HO} = \\vec {OL} \\implies L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"210\" height=\"19\" /> lies on Euler line of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Distances.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9a/Distances.png/350px-Distances.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"350\" height=\"213\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9a/Distances.png/525px-Distances.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9a/Distances.png/700px-Distances.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><i><b>Claim (Distance between projections)</b></i>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/9/0790d8cf4b7d8c4fbc199d673cbf6c0bbf568554.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x + y = a, c^2 – x^2 = h^2 = b^2 – y^2,\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c25fd7272fcef39543dddb21eb9b3cedd7cb106a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y^2 – x^2 = b^2 – c^2 \\implies y – x = \\frac {b^2 – c^2}{a},\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d4f8622a5e170e1e581305113e709c7dd52eb1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac {a}{2} –  \\frac {b^2 – c^2}{2a}, y = \\frac {a}{2} +  \\frac {b^2 – c^2}{2a}.\\]\" width=\"227\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Definition 2</b></i>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Longchamps_1.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/71/Longchamps_1.png/500px-Longchamps_1.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"323\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/71/Longchamps_1.png/750px-Longchamps_1.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/71/Longchamps_1.png/1000px-Longchamps_1.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>We call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/f/2df0d2004cb846c8d80abb3e4337626cbb55a79e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_A = A-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />circle of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f6f7cd16a47f33bebcf3fc361eeb808b630504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC.$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> The other two circles are defined symmetrically. The De Longchamps point of a triangle is the radical center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/722563bfd5e279d3115d6962b904fcdc85cce7f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A-$\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b179fc3cbe5f135dece01c0601a6db2be93ad866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B-$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />circle, and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/93875d269236b50fb99cd99249c0fa9b87eb6f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />circle of the triangle (Casey – 1886). Prove that De Longchamps point under this definition is the same as point under <i><b>Definition 1.</b></i>\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acf64e19498b0aac19e4ee04174a2e4a93109b1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H, G,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0ebb0cf67e023d45e33fe3b2d96f25f5013eb49d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> be orthocenter, centroid, and De Longchamps point, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8a61b8667b8ee0dbb1231aa0845a526438b73ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" /> cross <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/4297d316f37d78f87ceec82601e3c3ba1fee993a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710fb5fa3adedd7a16739e543d846747adbe05b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> The other points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/c/2fc36572cd4764cd29d4e19e656fd353163ac9b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(D, F, B&#39;, C&#39;)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" /> are defined symmetrically.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d59d840b53d1609bac438053d4a5ca0af8ead0f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB&#39; = BC, B&#39;C = AB \\implies \\triangle ABC = \\triangle CB&#39;A \\implies\\]\" width=\"413\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/5086f77f0bf4d667f970348895946bf10ba608f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB||B&#39;C \\implies CH \\perp B&#39;C.\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" />\nSimilarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d909fd68127348924655e339f201d7fe2d2b6b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH \\perp A&#39;C \\implies A&#39;B&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"177\" height=\"16\" /> is diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1aabceebe6e2bfbb4185034322d383dc8dec581.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_C \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/8/f6878a5dbfec7b53246970d4fe9af079111d4094.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle A&#39;EB&#39; = 90^\\circ, 2\\vec {BG} = \\vec {GB&#39;}.\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"21\" /> \n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a764854d1073fac0a788e874db580d732c7c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;$\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> is anticomplementary triangle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/449cefc476028b5577b1ed30e14b56c03a68f690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, \\triangle DEF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" /> is orthic triangle of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d0608222c465b48fe29c3b97dad1150c1189cae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" /> So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0ebb0cf67e023d45e33fe3b2d96f25f5013eb49d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> is orthocenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d0608222c465b48fe29c3b97dad1150c1189cae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51d1e4b9a239e637ceace7f5d8a996ecd050e33e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\vec {HG} = \\vec GL_o, 2\\vec {GO} = \\vec HG \\implies L_o = L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"307\" height=\"23\" /> as desired.\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"De_Longchamps_circle\">De Longchamps circle</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=De_Longchamps_point&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: De Longchamps circle\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>De Longchamps circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> of the obtuse triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is circle centered at de Longchamps point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> which is orthogonal to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3cd5d57cd4d2bf4d8189ea97403e7fb66dae53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"10\" /> Prove that de Longchamps circle is orthogonal to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/6/6d67bd431206bd26129a174133d8c0b254475c2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_A, \\omega_B, A-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />power, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b179fc3cbe5f135dece01c0601a6db2be93ad866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B-$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />power and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/93875d269236b50fb99cd99249c0fa9b87eb6f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />power cicles and the radius of de Longchamps circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc31084613f204e276e65db6cee1bd11bea0d0b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_{\\Omega} = 4R \\sqrt { – \\cos A \\cos B \\cos C}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"237\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Longchamps_circle.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e1/Longchamps_circle.png/350px-Longchamps_circle.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"350\" height=\"320\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e1/Longchamps_circle.png/525px-Longchamps_circle.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/e/e1/Longchamps_circle.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9266b48270fe1c410a1a90b4786b1ce0a7279aaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec {A&#39;B&#39;} = 2\\vec {BA}, A&#39;B&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"23\" /> – diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3cd5d57cd4d2bf4d8189ea97403e7fb66dae53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/9/ab9a6877fb748a421910c3317c8ac965f86abc48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/5/8a52f40afedf1c8727d71b0ad5a7ea0a7119b088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> be crosspoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/4297d316f37d78f87ceec82601e3c3ba1fee993a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b678555b8713a7a17de91456e65ec7614d2ceeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&#39; \\implies A&#39;E_0 \\perp AB&#39; \\implies E = E_0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"295\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are simmetric with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41cb7b1df9195680053dea51733d8d9980e2b144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC, MA&#39; = AM \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"178\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/722563bfd5e279d3115d6962b904fcdc85cce7f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A-$\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />power circle and on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/4297d316f37d78f87ceec82601e3c3ba1fee993a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c2e35454198cc759733326edf9ca1fba0854b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega \\perp \\omega_C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d06124ef16be66a700080c921c7160f9cc594d95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L, A&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/a/60a5ea8c13f5fc17819b791c1e4680a5c1a50bd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\Omega \\perp A-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" /> power circle.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the radical center of all six circles, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> is perpendicular to each of these circles.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is orthocenter of the anticomplementary triangle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> so radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> is twice radius of circle finded by Claim <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e362d40478030dc56ab9e55be492c5644b13455.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies R_{\\Omega} = 4R \\sqrt { – \\cos A \\cos B \\cos C}.\\]\" width=\"271\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Claim (Radius)</b></i>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Longchamps_Claim.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f7/Longchamps_Claim.png/300px-Longchamps_Claim.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"350\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f7/Longchamps_Claim.png/450px-Longchamps_Claim.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f7/Longchamps_Claim.png/600px-Longchamps_Claim.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be obtuse triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afdc127dec13b922f70460cb3569b00f3c75604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\angle A &gt; 90^\\circ)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> with circumcircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/85955932018c71ba9f22e9b97cafda1c5da07b9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> circumradius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a1603310a6bfb8542204de0e46b0e4484d3897a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and orthocenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e852702a676b21d2bcd9820a3e570a5765ef6e7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0b5243f7e525a53836ea34c8a49486dace660f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the circle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecee609050b0744995a1b79ec0fcd162a97441b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB.$\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the circle perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0b5243f7e525a53836ea34c8a49486dace660f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e852702a676b21d2bcd9820a3e570a5765ef6e7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd0b7e45d3e274cef324a6a0da3b12902cc73cbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_\\omega,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> the radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" />\n</p><p>Let altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3ddf9a5fa2fca5c4787d4f989af0eef1387bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> cross <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and cross <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> second time at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/6/dd600103cd7b80e823f2c530613ace675ad8a60f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da8ce1ad3a5aed5d2b5d7a6d02063238bf199fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD \\perp BD \\implies D \\in \\omega&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"19\" /> points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ff6b0867888ef6a1062b2221874dae6336c1962.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H,A, D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> are collinear <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef48ac956824fcaea163a530a717e6df694aa006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"9\" />\n</p><p>Inversion with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> swap <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/8/868e32d1285b8737fed77a22ae3578eaf71bf2be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D \\implies R_\\omega^2 = HA \\cdot HD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Well known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/d/96d814b96fc0a4763b3400e5c8382e769051e964.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HA = – 2R \\cos A.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b69917a007b906d5073befb607d10ead6c06cf1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BC \\perp HD, AC \\perp BH \\implies \\angle C = \\angle BHD \\implies HD = BH \\cos C.\\]\" width=\"521\" height=\"16\" />\nPoints <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f783df024abc16be6be7f4d262c926e8f24fc6a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H&#39;$\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are symmetric with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4b34f689ee876f5aeb3ce41a020ca732f4562fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC \\implies BH&#39; = BH.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c06815b73d84064a6312c7dc4bb73daed8671e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BAH&#39; = 90^\\circ – \\angle B \\implies BH&#39; = 2R \\sin \\angle BAH&#39; = 2R \\cos B \\implies\\]\" width=\"503\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9d27757bcad0eb127a89d2dadb7b43976584b79.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R_\\omega^2 = – 2R \\cos A \\cdot 2R \\cos B \\cos C \\implies R_\\omega = 2R \\sqrt{– \\cos A \\cos B \\cos C}.\\]\" width=\"523\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"De_Longchamps_line\">De Longchamps line</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=De_Longchamps_point&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: De Longchamps line\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Longchamps_lime.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/27/Longchamps_lime.png/450px-Longchamps_lime.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"284\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/27/Longchamps_lime.png/675px-Longchamps_lime.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/27/Longchamps_lime.png/900px-Longchamps_lime.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>The de Longchamps line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is defined as the radical axes of the de Longchamps circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and of the circumscribed circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/0/9502deda051c9fb2143b9aba51a31cc43684d65e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega&#39;$\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> (the anticomplementary triangle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22e4ea136c37e6d2b30f5c5574c333b4a33d7cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0b5243f7e525a53836ea34c8a49486dace660f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (centroid of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />) with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/baf383f3f95682e36ce8c3daba35c0c627b91b87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rho = \\frac {\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sqrt {a^2 + b^2 + c^2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"43\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5f7dc1d5eeb07dd8b66defdcdc5e92fafab1d61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = BC, b = AC, c = AB.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Prove that the de Longchamps line is perpendicular to Euler line and is the radical axes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af01e44fe4ede9c07d14eb4e0303cfcc9ec22a6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega, \\Omega&#39;, \\omega,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e1fddc21cda84fd000da3f926f4685ebcafad1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>Center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, center of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/b/cbb9d474825a55e039b9eb258942b63138936dbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L \\implies OL \\perp l,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/988eb7862af325a152533cff8375694dd9078fda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OL$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is Euler line.\nThe homothety with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> maps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbfcc9387fbb18001978e0b89ee1133b7be0080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF.$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> This homothety maps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11f3927f617b1ee61f7fb2f4cfcf9e9bd72e05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2feabae9785b5ed065decdf0dc39b13b35cef57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_{\\Omega} \\ne R_{\\Omega&#39;}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c22e7d091a8d248d2e547e2030cf67cd631a66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega \\cap \\Omega&#39; = K \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"16\" /> there is two inversion which swap <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11f3927f617b1ee61f7fb2f4cfcf9e9bd72e05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> \n</p><p>First inversion <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/0/640d742cf5fecc5451d7ebb3a255d335493ef847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_{\\omega&#39;}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> centered at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/93051c920c666fdb1f6070c8b3f689919930d7eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G = \\frac {\\vec O \\cdot 2R + \\vec H \\cdot R}{2R + R} = \\frac {2\\vec O + \\vec H}{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"256\" height=\"46\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the point of crossing  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11f3927f617b1ee61f7fb2f4cfcf9e9bd72e05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>The radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0b5243f7e525a53836ea34c8a49486dace660f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> we can find using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b23afcf516eee07b46a95b29f9d251320600a4c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle HKO:$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c976a796815b9d6d8d9bbf5b9bb8539ec195ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OK = R, HK = 2R, HG = 2GO \\implies GK^2 = 2(R^2 – GO^2), GO^2 = \\frac {HO^2}{9} \\implies\\]\" width=\"610\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79ebf241578cc739d15a7f9c49269f1e064791ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R_G = GK = \\frac {\\sqrt {2(a^2 + b^2 + c^2)}}{3}.\\]\" width=\"244\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Second inversion <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba718250592d387b3651b8aa95430e96df76ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_{\\omega}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> centered at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/b/e8b2841b9834c08e819687805113f2463772a7fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L = \\frac {\\vec O \\cdot 2R – \\vec H \\cdot R}{2R – R} = 2 \\vec O – \\vec H.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"225\" height=\"44\" /> We can make the same calculations and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0f28c7e705b0aa3b12fae4c7bf1f6bd6a01f8b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_L = 4R \\sqrt{– \\cos A \\cos B \\cos C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"231\" height=\"23\" /> as desired.\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=De_Longchamps_point&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcircle\" title=\"Circumcircle\">Circumcircle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euler_line\" title=\"Euler line\">Euler line</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=De_Longchamps_point&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018082148\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.087 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.158 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 960/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 951/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 281/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 33277/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   54.005      1 -total\n 23.79%   12.849      1 Template:Asy_image\n 18.87%   10.191      1 Template:Title_restriction\n 15.14%    8.179      1 Template:Stub\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6066:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018082148 and revision id 243782. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}